__pycache__/

# Rendered frame sequences. One PNG per frame at 30fps, which is the rate the
# Remotion timeline indexes them at, and one render per aspect ratio: the two
# inserts come to 1,647 files. They are reproducible from `npm run film` and do
# not belong in source.
#
# 30 and not the 60 brief §5.2 asks for. Remotion consumes the sequence by frame
# number against a 30fps composition, so a 60fps sequence would either play at
# half speed or drop every second frame, and neither is a thing anybody would
# choose. Manim's own rounding is why the counts are read back off disk rather
# than computed: an 8-second insert is 255 frames, not 240.
out/
